loopHeld: the iterator of the for loop of its making frame, fresh (queue 339: holdLoopGen; closed when the loop pops it)"] [58 1 "// genExt is a generator's rare fields."] [60 2 "// origin is cr_origin: the frames that created a coroutine while origin tracking was on, nil otherwise"] [62 2 "// finalizer is sys's asyncgen finalizer hook at its first use (ag_origin_or_finalizer), nil when none"] [64 2 "// name, qualname: the objects assigned to __name__ and __qualname__, nil until then"] [68 1 "// more is g's rare fields, made when absent."] [86 1 "// newGenerator is a call's object of a function whose code is a generator's, a coroutine's or an"] [87 1 "// async generator's: f bound, not run."] [100 3 "// a coroutine never awaited warns at its death (_PyGen_Finalize; queue 218): tracked only if still not started"] [101 3 "// when the pending list is flushed (most are awaited at once)"] [109 1 "// genThrow is an exception thrown into a suspended frame: the resumption runs the frame's yield-value or yield-from"] [110 1 "// again (its PC set back to Lasti), which finds it here and raises it there, so the frame's handlers see it at the"] [111 1 "// suspension point. Its delegate has had it by then (_gen_throw, throwArgs). One thread runs at a time, and the frame's"] [112 1 "// first instruction run is that one."] [118 1 "// genDone is the outcome of a delegate resume ran itself for a frame suspended at its yield-from (queue 330, passDelegate):"] [119 1 "// the frame goes on from its yield-from, whose instruction finds it here as its send's outcome (what the delegate yielded,"] [120 1 "// returned or raised). One thread runs at a time, and the frame's first instruction run is that one."] [127 1 "// passDelegate is the delegate a resumption of g with a sent value hands the value to without running g's frame (queue 330:"] [128 1 "// CPython's SEND_GEN runs a chain of yield-froms in one loop, pyi's resume ran each level's frame, its loop and its"] [129 1 "// instruction): g's frame suspended at its yield-from on a generator or coroutine, no tool's events, no eval breaker"] [130 1 "// pending, no throw pending for the frame, and the depths below their limits, so that the frame's own resumption would"] [131 1 "// have done nothing before its yield-from sent the value on; nil otherwise."] [145 1 "// genSuspendedAt is the operation f is suspended at, when it is."] [153 1 "// yieldFrom is the delegate the generator is suspended in (gi_yieldfrom), or nil."] [161 1 "// resume runs g with v sent into it (exc nil) or exc raised in it (gen_send_ex2; closing: gen_close's, silent on an"] [162 1 "// exhausted coroutine): the value it yields (yielded non-nil), or the value it returns (returned, the generator"] [163 1 "// finished), or what it raises (err; a StopIteration raised in it is a RuntimeError, PEP 479)."] [182 2 "// a throw nested in this one before its frame took it (a finalizer the frame's start drains closes another"] [183 2 "// generator: queue 297) leaves this one's in place when it is done"] [186 37 "// sent into after a yield (its RESUME's eval breaker raised in it)"] [187 2 "// suspended at a yield-from: RESUME_AFTER_YIELD_FROM checks no eval breaker, the delegate's own resumption does"] [192 4 "// raised at its RESUME: its frame in the traceback, the generator finished"] [208 2 "// the generator's own exception slot over the resuming level's (gi_exc_state pushed on the exc_info stack)"] [219 3 "// queue 330: the value sent on to the delegate here, f entered as run enters it (f_back, the depths, the thread's"] [220 3 "// frame) and running its yield-from (f.PC past it), as its own run would have done before the delegate's"] [232 4 "// the delegate yielded: so does f, from its yield-from (opYieldFrom), as the loop returns a suspended frame"] [240 4 "// the delegate is done (or a tool's events came on): f goes on from its yield-from with that outcome, past its"] [241 4 "// RESUME (it was resumed before the delegate ran)"] [242 24 "// another frame's, should a tool's callback run before f's yield-from took it"] [262 32 "// not kept past the pop: the exception it was (py-final-1126)"] [267 3 "// a generator suspended where a handler can see close()'s GeneratorExit is closed at its death (queue 218)"] [277 15 "// an exhausted generator's frame has no caller"] [285 1 "// stopIterationError is PEP 479's RuntimeError for a StopIteration (or, in an async generator, a"] [286 1 "// StopAsyncIteration) raised out of g's frame: its cause and context the exception, its traceback empty"] [287 1 "// (CPython's INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR, re-raised out of the frame)."] [303 2 "// no entry of g's frame (queue 330: CPython's INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR makes it in the frame's handler and"] [304 2 "// RERAISE adds none; the StopIteration, its cause, has the frame's)"] [309 1 "// newStopIteration is StopIteration(v), with no arguments when v is None (gen_send_ex's)."] [317 1 "// stopIterationValue is a raised StopIteration's value (_PyGen_FetchStopIterationValue), ok false when"] [318 1 "// err is not one."] [330 1 "// isRaised is err a raised exception of type typ (or a subtype)."] [336 1 "// send is g.send(v): what it yields, or StopIteration with what it returns."] [348 1 "// throwRaised is gen_send_ex with an exception set: err raised in g's frame (a Go error that is no exception as it is)."] [357 1 "// excMatches is PyErr_GivenExceptionMatches of a class or an instance."] [365 1 "// throwArgs is _gen_throw: typ, val and tb as given (nil: not given), first to the delegate; closeOnGenExit false is"] [366 1 "// an async generator's aclose and athrow, whose GeneratorExit is thrown into the delegate. An error in the arguments"] [367 1 "// leaves g suspended."] [386 5 "// the frame linked into the stack, for complete backtraces"] [417 2 "// throw_here"] [442 1 "// normalizeException is PyErr_NormalizeException of a class and a value: the instance, or the exception making it"] [443 1 "// raised (which takes its place)."] [469 1 "// genThrowMethod is gen_throw: the arguments' count and deprecation, then _gen_throw."] [492 1 "// throw is g.throw(...)."] [504 1 "// close is g.close() (gen_close): GeneratorExit thrown in, or what closing its delegate raised; its return value when"] [505 1 "// it returns."] [544 1 "// genSendTo is a send into an iterator delegated to (SEND): a generator's or coroutine's resume, else"] [545 1 "// __next__ when v is None, else its send method; yielded non-nil, or the value it returned (a"] [546 1 "// StopIteration's, or None at an iterator's end)."] [551 40 "// FutureIter_am_send: no StopIteration made"] [555 50 "// PyIter_Send: tp_iternext when it has one"] [557 4 "// a class's __next__ (slot_tp_iternext): its StopIteration's value is the delegate's return (queue 330: the slot"] [558 4 "// ends the for-iter's way, without it)"] [585 1 "// genCloseIter closes a delegate (gen_close_iter): a generator's or coroutine's close, else its close method when it"] [586 1 "// has one."] [604 1 "// asyncGenWrapped is a value an async generator yields (CPython's _PyAsyncGenWrappedValue): its asend"] [605 1 "// and athrow see it apart from the values its awaits yield to the event loop."] [610 1 "// opYieldValue is yield-value: the value popped and yielded (wrapped in an async generator), f kept"] [611 1 "// suspended; resumed, the value sent is on the stack (pushed by resume), or an exception thrown in is"] [612 1 "// raised here."] [628 1 "// chainStackItem is _PyErr_ChainStackItem (gen_send_ex2 with an exception, queue 223): an exception thrown into a"] [629 1 "// generator's frame takes the exception being handled as its __context__ (_PyErr_SetObject's chaining) when the"] [630 1 "// generator's own exception state, pushed at its resumption, holds one."] [639 1 "// opYieldFrom is yield-from ([receiver value] -> its return value): CPython's SEND, YIELD_VALUE and"] [640 1 "// END_SEND loop as one operation. Each value the receiver yields suspends f with the instruction run"] [641 1 "// again on resumption (PC set back to it), the receiver kept below and the sent value pushed on it."] [646 3 "// the delegate resume sent the value to itself (queue 330, passDelegate): its outcome is this send's"] [649 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [659 3 "// CLEANUP_THROW: a StopIteration is the delegate's end, its value this expression's; anything else is raised here"] [662 11 "// the placeholder resume pushed"] [681 54 "// the delegate's end: STOP_ITERATION, or RAISE (queue 219t)"] [692 1 "// opGetYieldFromIter is get-yield-from-iter: a generator or a coroutine as it is (a coroutine only in a"] [693 1 "// coroutine's code), else iter(o)."] [712 1 "// genMethods are the methods of the types of PY5d's files, put into their dictionaries by d5Ready"] [713 1 "// (lazily: a dictionary's keys need str's hash, which str.go's init sets after these files' inits)."] [720 1 "// d5Method declares a method of a type of PY5d's: name in t's dictionary as a built-in method."] [731 1 "// d5Ready fills the dictionaries of PY5d's types with their methods, once (each of their GetAttr"] [732 1 "// slots and operations calls it first)."] [753 1 "// d5GetAttr is the GetAttr slot of PY5d's types: their methods ready, then extra (attributes not in"] [754 1 "// the dictionary), then object's lookup."] [767 1 "// d5Args checks a method's argument count: between min and max positional, no keywords."] [783 1 "// coroOriginDepth is sys.set_coroutine_origin_tracking_depth's depth (0: off)."] [786 1 "// coroOrigin is compute_cr_origin: (filename, lineno, function name) of the creating frame and up to depth-1 of its"] [787 1 "// callers, innermost first."] [803 1 "// genRepr is \"<KIND object QUALNAME at 0x...>\", the address an identity number."] [810 1 "// genGetSets declares the attributes of a generator, coroutine or async generator (prefix gi_, cr_ or ag_; delegate"] [811 1 "// the attribute's name for gi_yieldfrom, cr_await, ag_await)."] [853 40 "// a for 